---
import "../styles/global.css";
import "../styles/tactile.css";

const pageTitle = "Contact RNG Chords | Jonathan R. Reed Music Tool";
const pageDescription =
	"Contact Jonathan R. Reed about RNG Chords, the free browser-based chord progression generator for songwriting and MIDI sketching.";
const pageUrl = Astro.site ? new URL("/contact/", Astro.site).toString() : undefined;
const socialImage = Astro.site
	? new URL("/social-card.svg", Astro.site).toString()
	: "/social-card.svg";
const publishedDate = "2026-04-21";
const modifiedDate = "2026-08-04";
const structuredData = {
	"@context": "https://schema.org",
	"@type": "ContactPage",
	name: "Contact RNG Chords",
	description: pageDescription,
	...(pageUrl ? { url: pageUrl } : {}),
	datePublished: publishedDate,
	dateModified: modifiedDate,
	author: {
		"@type": "Person",
		name: "Jonathan R. Reed",
		url: "https://jonathanrreed.com",
	},
};
---

<html lang="en">
	<head>
		<meta charset="utf-8" />
		<script is:inline>try{var t=JSON.parse(localStorage.getItem("rng-chords-creative-session")||"{}").tableTheme;if(t)document.documentElement.setAttribute("data-theme",t);}catch(e){}</script>
		<link rel="icon" href="/favicon.ico" sizes="any">
		<link rel="icon" type="image/png" sizes="32x32" href="/favicon-32x32.png">
		<link rel="icon" type="image/png" sizes="16x16" href="/favicon-16x16.png">
		<link rel="apple-touch-icon" sizes="180x180" href="/apple-touch-icon-180x180.png">
		<link rel="manifest" href="/site.webmanifest">
		<meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1" />
		<meta name="generator" content={Astro.generator} />
		<meta name="theme-color" content="#0b0706" />
		<meta name="description" content={pageDescription} />
		<meta property="og:type" content="website" />
		<meta property="og:title" content={pageTitle} />
		<meta property="og:description" content={pageDescription} />
		<meta property="og:image" content={socialImage} />
		<meta name="twitter:card" content="summary_large_image" />
		<meta name="twitter:title" content={pageTitle} />
		<meta name="twitter:description" content={pageDescription} />
		<meta name="twitter:image" content={socialImage} />
		{pageUrl ? <link rel="canonical" href={pageUrl} /> : null}
		{pageUrl ? <meta property="og:url" content={pageUrl} /> : null}
		<link rel="preconnect" href="https://fonts.googleapis.com" />
		<link rel="preconnect" href="https://fonts.gstatic.com" crossorigin />
		<link
			href="https://fonts.googleapis.com/css2?family=Cormorant+Garamond:wght@500;600;700&family=Manrope:wght@400;500;600;700;800&display=swap"
			rel="stylesheet"
		/>
		<title>{pageTitle}</title>
		<script
			is:inline
			type="application/ld+json"
			set:html={JSON.stringify(structuredData).replace(/</g, "\\u003c")}
		/>
	</head>
	<body>
		<main class="info-page">
			<a class="info-page__back" href="/">RNG Chords</a>
			<nav class="sr-only" aria-label="RNG Chords utility pages">
				<a href="/">RNG Chords generator</a>
				<a href="/about/">About RNG Chords</a>
				<a href="/privacy/">RNG Chords privacy policy</a>
			</nav>
			<section class="info-page__panel panel-surface">
				<p class="panel-title__eyebrow">Contact</p>
				<h1>Contact Jonathan about RNG Chords.</h1>
				<p>
					Feedback, bug reports, accessibility problems, and feature ideas for
					RNG Chords all go through Jonathan R. Reed's main contact page.
				</p>
				<p>
					If something broke, tell me the browser, whether playback ever started,
					which instrument was selected, and what you were doing when it went
					wrong: rolling chords, keeping a progression, copying text, or
					exporting MIDI.
				</p>
				<p>
					A progression that just sounds bad is a different report. Include the
					mode, key, instrument, tempo, and any chords you had kept. For a failed
					export, say whether the file was headed for a DAW, notation software,
					or storage. That is the fastest way to tell a musical complaint apart
					from a browser bug.
				</p>
				<p>
					Accessibility notes are welcome, and I would rather hear them early.
					Keyboard navigation, focus order, control labels, the playback
					controls, reduced motion, and phone screens are the places most likely
					to have something wrong with them.
				</p>
				<p>
					For feature ideas, describe the musical problem instead of naming a
					control. "I need more borrowed chords in minor keys" or "I want a
					cleaner way to practice ii V I movement" tells me far more than a
					request for more randomness. Same with teaching: if you use this in a
					lesson or a rehearsal, mention the level and the exercise.
				</p>
				<p>
					Short notes are fine. What you expected, what happened, and what it did
					to the thing you were working on.
				</p>
				<p>
					<a class="info-page__button" href="https://jonathanrreed.com/contact/">
						Open Jonathan's contact page
					</a>
				</p>
				<p class="info-page__meta">
					Published <time datetime={publishedDate}>April 21, 2026</time>.
				</p>
			</section>
		</main>
	</body>
</html>
